602 - O Brother, Be Faithful
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 602
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[G]O broth[C]er, be [G]faithful! Soon [C]Jesus will [G]come,
For [C]whom we have [G]waited so [D]long;
[D7]O, [G]soon [C]we shall [G]enter our [C]glorious [G]home,
And join in the [Am]con[D7]queror’s [G]song.
O [D]brother, be [D7]faithful! For [G]why should [D7]we [G]prove
Unfaithful to Him who hath [D]shown
[D7]Such [G]deep, [C]such un[G]bounded and [C]infinite [G]love—
Who died to re[Am]deem [D7]us His [G]own.

Verse 2:
[G]O [C]brother be [G]faithful! [C]the city [G]of gold,
[C]Prepared for [G]the good [D]and the blest,
[D7]Is [G]waiting [C]its portals [G]of [C]pearl [G]to unfold,
[Am]And welcome [D7]thee into [G]thy rest.
[D]Then, [D7]brother be [G]faithful! not [D7]long shall [G]we stay
[D]In weariness here, and forlorn,
[D7]Time's [G]dark [C]night of [G]sorrow [C]is [G]wearing away,
[Am]We haste [D7]to the [G]glorious morn.

Verse 3:
[G]O [C]brother be [G]faithful! [C]He soon [G]will descend,
[C]Creation's [G]omnipotent [D]King,
[D7]While [G]legions [C]of [G]angels [C]His [G]chariot attend,
[Am]And palm [D7]wreaths, of [G]victory bring.
[D]O [D7]brother be [G]faithful! and [D7]soon shalt [G]thou hear
[D]They Savior pronounce the glad word,
[D7]Well [G]done, [C]faithful servant, [G]they [C]title [G]is clear,
[Am]To enter [D7]the joy [G]of thy Lord.

Verse 4:
[G]O [C]brother [G]be [C]faithful! [G]eternity's years
[C]Shall tell [G]for thy [D]faithfulness now,
[D7]When [G]bright smiles [C]of [G]gladness shall [C]scatter [G]thy tears,
[Am]A coronet [D7]gleam on [G]thy brow.
[D]O [D7]brother be [G]faithful! [D7]the promise [G]is sure,
[D]That waits for the faithful and tried;
[D7]To [G]reign [C]with the [G]ransomed, [C]immortal [G]and pure,
[Am]And [D7]ever with [G]Jesus abide.
